# Testing — vitest, colocated, AAA

## Context

Tests use vitest and live NEXT TO the code they cover (e.g.
`app/src/reducer.test.ts` beside `app/src/reducer.ts`). Run with
`cd app && npm test`. See existing `reducer.test.ts` / `store.test.ts` for style.

## Rule

- Colocate every test beside the file under test, named `<name>.test.ts`,
  `<name>.spec.ts`, `<name>.test.tsx`, or `<name>.spec.tsx`.
- Import from vitest: `import { describe, expect, it } from "vitest";`.
- Structure each test Arrange → Act → Assert (AAA); keep one behavior per `it`.
- When you add an action/reducer case or a `lib/` helper, ADD a colocated test
  in the same change.
- Assert on returned NEW state; also assert immutability where relevant
  (previous state unchanged, `next !== prev`).
- Keep the seeded tests green — never weaken an assertion to make code pass.

## How to verify

1. Each new `*.{test,spec}.{ts,tsx}` sits beside its source file.
2. `cd app && npm test` is green, including the new tests.
3. New reducer/action/helper code has at least one covering test.




